    tldr: "The inherited BRCA test that decides who can have PARP inhibitor pills for ovarian, breast, pancreatic and prostate cancer.",
    summary: "Approved 19 December 2014 (PMA P140020) as the companion diagnostic for olaparib in germline BRCA-mutated advanced ovarian cancer, the first FDA-approved companion diagnostic based on an inherited variant. Claims followed for olaparib and talazoparib in HER2-negative metastatic breast cancer (2018), olaparib maintenance in first-line ovarian cancer (SOLO-1, 2018), pancreatic cancer (POLO, 2019), metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer (PROfound, 2020) and early breast cancer (OlympiA, 2022). Myriad's monopoly on BRCA testing ended with the 2013 US Supreme Court ruling that isolated genes cannot be patented, and multi-gene hereditary panels have since become the norm, but BRACAnalysis CDx remains the labelled test.",
